{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Torsion.HeckeMassElement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Torsion.HeckeMassElement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Ring.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.mass_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.mass_exact","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L109-L123","doc":"Exact mass decomposition for non-negative real components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.mass_upper_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.mass_upper_bound","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L99-L107","doc":"The mass decomposes via the triangle inequality, with equality\nwhen descended and transient components are non-negative reals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.mass","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L85-L97","doc":"**Post-Arch Archimedean mass.**\n\nThe categorical mass equals the Archimedean norm of the mass\nelement (standing in for `‖tr_M(Φ_mass)‖`).  Requires\n`[NormedCommRing R]`; lives downstream of the formal chain.\n\nPer `QOU.GroundRingAnnotations`, this is **not** part of the\npre-Arch chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.frobeniusMassSquared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.frobeniusMassSquared","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**Pre-Arch Frobenius mass squared.**\n\n`m²(Φ) := ⟨Φ.massElement, Φ.massElement⟩_F`, where the Frobenius\npairing is supplied by the caller.  Valued in `R` (no Archimedean\nnorm). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Decomposition: Φ_mass = Φ^desc + Φ^trans. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.massElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.massElement","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The mass element is the sum of descended and transient components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.transientComponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.transientComponent","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The transient component Φ^trans (blow-up contributions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.descendedComponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.descendedComponent","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The descended component Φ^desc (base-level cycle). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.particleElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.particleElement","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The particle's Hecke element ρ(β) (before Frobenius dressing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.HeckeMassElement","kind":"structure","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/HeckeMassElement.lean#L47-L72","doc":"The Hecke mass element: given a particle's Hecke element ρ(β)\nand the Frobenius–comultiplication dressing, the mass element\nis the dressed element whose Markov trace computes the mass.\n\nAbstractly: Φ_mass(β) = τ(L_{α_ϱ}) where\nα_ϱ = (∫_A ⊗ id) ∘ Δ ∘ ϱ and L denotes left multiplication\nin the Frobenius–Hopf algebra.\n\nWe encode this as a structure carrying the decomposition data,\npolymorphic in the ground ring `R` (pre-Arch: `R = ℤ[q^±1]`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}